1
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:03,500
你不是才给他剪过头发吗
Didn't you just cut his hair?

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:06,959
对 但今天是他的幼儿园毕业派对
Yes, but it's his kindergarten graduation party today.

3
00:00:06,959 --> 00:00:09,608
好了 告别不要搂搂抱抱 我走了
Okay, no messy goodbyes, I'm out of here.

4
00:00:09,608 --> 00:00:11,980
宝贝 我会想死你的
Ay, papi, I'm going to miss you.

5
00:00:11,980 --> 00:00:15,060
你能不能至少留下来参加我为乔办的派对
Can you at least stay for the party that I'm making for Joe?

6
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,860
妈妈 努斯鲍姆太太花钱雇我
Mom, Mrs. Nussbaum is paying me

7
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,680
在周五中午前帮她把车开到特拉华州
to get her car to Delaware by Friday at noon.

8
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,700
我已经浪费了一小时找我的驾驶手套
I already lost an hour looking for my driving gloves.

9
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,140
你要开着辆毛毛虫绿的丰田凯美瑞
You're plowing through the heartlands

10
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,760
穿过民风剽悍的中部
in an inchworm-green Camry

11
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:25,740
车尾贴还写着"吃肉等同谋杀"
with a bumper sticker that says "Meat is Murder."

12
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,620
我是故意把这副手套藏起来的
I hid these gloves for a reason.

13
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:32,100
听着 叫你当心点可不是玩笑话
Listen, uh, we weren't kidding about you being careful.

14
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:35,960
不是我夸张 记得要提高警惕
And, uh, not to get dramatic, just keep your wits about you.

15
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:36,680
给
Here.

16
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:38,460
这是什么鬼
What the hell is that?

17
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:40,120
还能是空气清新剂吗 你说是什么
It's an air freshener. What does it look like?

18
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:41,740
我是要去玛莎·斯图尔特的
I'm going on the Martha Stewart

19
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:43,100
美国民宿之旅
bed-and-breakfast tour of America,

20
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:44,800
又不是探索男子气概土著之旅
not an Aboriginal manhood quest.

21
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:46,180
我没说你会用得到
I'm not saying you're gonna need it,

22
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:47,580
只是有备无患
just better safe than sorry.

23
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:49,040
划就行 千万别用捅的
Slash, don't stab.

24
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:53,140
别动来动去 我快好啦
Stop wiggling. I'm almost done.

25
00:00:55,610 --> 00:00:57,291
你干嘛倒抽一口气
Why'd you gasp?

26
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,920
不要 头发是我的身份象征啊
Ah! My hair is my identity!

27
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:18,840
小卡 看来我还是得干个活
Uh, Cam? Uh, turns out I have to do that work thing after all.

28
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:19,860
我们在乔的派对上见好吗
I'll meet you at Joe's party?

29
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:22,380
好的 卡尔 过来抱抱你米奇尔舅舅
Oh, okay. Cal, come give your Uncle Mitchell a hug.

30
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:23,160
抱抱
Hug!

31
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:25,320
不 不要抱抱 他人呢
No. No, no hug. No -- where is he?

32
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:27,151
他从哪个方向跑来 哪个方向
Which way is he coming from? Coming from?

33
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:31,440
小卡姐姐的儿子现在暂住我们家
Cam's sister's son is staying with us

34
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:33,020
因为 你们懂的 她又被关进监狱了
because, well, you know, she's back in jail.

35
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,580
但她没做什么大坏事
But she didn't do anything terrible.

36
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,100
她只是不明白
She just didn't understand

37
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,061
她上次坐牢的假释条款 她...
the rules of her probation from last time, when --

38
00:01:38,061 --> 00:01:39,660
她上次做了一些小坏事
When she did something a little terrible.

39
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:41,600
但我们准备把小卡尔
But we're taking baby Cal back to

40
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:43,000
送回农场跟我父母住
live with my parents on the farm.

41
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,600
这是好事 因为他并不是...
Which is a good thing because he's not really a --

42
00:01:45,736 --> 00:01:46,479
适合家养的宝宝
a house baby.

43
00:01:46,479 --> 00:01:49,680
真不是 他力气大得惊人 块头大到破表
No, no, he's freakishly strong and off the charts size-wise.

44
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,440
没有破表啦 数一数二而已啦
On the charts. 99th percentile.

45
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:54,560
他只有两颗牙 但我见过他吃掉整只鸡
He has two teeth and I've seen him eat a whole chicken.

46
00:01:55,417 --> 00:01:56,740
好了 我得走了
All right, I got to go.

47
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:58,060
等等 给我的抱抱呢
Wait, where's my hug?

48
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,080
-抱抱 -走 快走 快逃命
- Hug! - Go! Go! Save yourself!

49
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:06,797
我们的戏服在后座
Our costumes are in the back.

50
00:02:06,797 --> 00:02:08,260
菲尔和我要去参加英雄展
Phil and I are going to Hero-Con

51
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:10,862
放纵我们对奇幻小说的热爱
to indulge in our love of fantasy fiction.

52
00:02:10,862 --> 00:02:12,157
我一直都很想去
Um, I-I've always wanted to go,

53
00:02:12,157 --> 00:02:13,920
但这个展会偏宅男向
but I-it's a little nerd-forward,

54
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:16,300
我以前总担心我家人会取笑我
and I was always afraid my family would make fun of me.

55
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:17,960
所以我叫菲尔保守这个秘密
So I've asked Phil to keep it between us.

56
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:20,140
所以我们选了秘密的战士暗号
That's why we chose our secret warrior signal.

57
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:22,085
我第一个提议是吹维京号角
My first suggestion was to blow a Viking horn.

58
00:02:22,085 --> 00:02:23,280
-对了 千万别上网搜 -已经搜了
- Don't ever Google that, by the way. - I already did.

59
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:26,480
今年 我们最喜欢的剧要办见面座谈会
This year, there's a panel, um, on our favorite show,

60
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,480
《神剑之战》
"Clash of Swords."

61
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:30,740
这剧含有大量暴力情节和女性裸体
It's got a lot of graphic violence and female nudity,

62
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:32,100
但那也正合每个男人体内的
but that's part of its appeal

63
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:34,840
勇猛战士的胃口
to the fierce warrior inside every man.

64
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,040
我的眼线一直晕开
My eyeliner keeps smudging.

65
00:02:37,180 --> 00:02:38,540
真是"谢谢"你的推荐啊 彩妆专柜柜姐
Thanks a lot, gal at the MAC counter.

66
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,460
管他呢 我们看起来帅极了
Who cares? We look great.

67
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:41,240
我们上吧
Let's do this!

68
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:44,380
要记得我们把可靠的坐骑停在了22B
Just remember we left our trusty steed in section 22B.

69
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,220
我做不到 菲尔
I can't do it, Phil.

70
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,460
好吧 我可以写下来
Oh, okay. I can write it down.

71
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,299
不不 我以为我准备好了 但其实没有
No, no. I-I-I thought I was ready, but I'm not.

72
00:02:50,299 --> 00:02:52,781
我没准备好 我幻想了要来这么久
I'm not. I-I've fantasized so long about coming,

73
00:02:52,781 --> 00:02:54,778
现在我们真的来了 我却
and now that -- that we're here, I am...

74
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:58,240
我却感到羞愧 我都是40岁的老男人了
I'm mortified, okay? I'm a 40-year-old man.

75
00:02:58,340 --> 00:02:59,600
你才不是
No, you're not.

76
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,060
你是个390岁的高地北境人
You're a 390-year-old Highland Norph.

77
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:03,560
跟着一名职业勇士入场
And you're walking in with a lifer.

78
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:08,000
这宝贝能让我们畅行无阻 还送两杯蜂蜜酒
This baby gets us all-access and two free yards of mead.

79
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:11,020
你的命运就在那些门背后
Through those doors lies your destiny.

80
00:03:11,142 --> 00:03:13,118
"勇敢"用盖尔德语怎么说
What's the Galderean word for "Bravery"?

81
00:03:13,148 --> 00:03:14,050
辣个汤尼
Lochtani.

82
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:15,712
-再说一遍 -辣个汤尼
- Again! - Lochtani.

83
00:03:15,712 --> 00:03:18,337
嘛哩嘛哩哄
Namu oponggi su-whi-gorth!

84
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:20,638
你有看到玛格丽特吗
Have you seen Margaret?

85
00:03:20,638 --> 00:03:21,940
我要她把我今天的日程排开
I need her to clear my day.

86
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:24,090
我刚发现可以在网上收看高尔夫频道
I just found out you can get the Golf Channel online.

87
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:25,980
没有 她又请病假了
Nope, she's out sick again.

88
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,381
爸爸 别忘了我们要跟
Oh, Dad, don't forget we're about to meet with

89
00:03:27,381 --> 00:03:28,958
那所新企业的人见面
those guys from that start-up.

90
00:03:28,958 --> 00:03:31,280
对哦 一群有抱负的衣柜界新丁
Oh, right, aspiring closeteers

91
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:33,220
想向行业传奇寻求建议
seeking advice from an industry legend.

92
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:35,240
是的 记得要跳过那一段
Yeah, just skip that part of your speech

93
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:37,060
就是你说"不是我选择了衣柜..."
where you say "I didn't choose closets --"

94
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:38,500
是衣柜选择了我
They chose me!

95
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:41,720
我们不知道该把羽绒背心挂在哪儿
...We didn't know where to hang up our puffer vests,

96
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:44,197
于是就随便丢在某人桌上了
so we just dropped them on some rando's desk.

97
00:03:44,197 --> 00:03:46,620
你好 你们就是伊瑟拉视界的人吧
Hi. You must be the guys from EzraVision.

98
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:48,540
没错 我是尼克 这些是我的员工
Yes, I am Nick. And these are my guys.

99
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:49,960
不用说 我就是杰·普里契特
Jay Pritchett, obviously.

100
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:52,240
各位请坐 不要拘束
Fellas, take a seat. Make yourself comfortable.

101
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,300
哪一位负责拿录音机记录
Which one is gonna be holding the tape recorder?

102
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:55,780
这样吧 不如我们速战速决
You know what? Why don't we just make this quick?

103
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,540
我们等下还得去车行逛逛
We actually have to go hang out in a bike shop

104
00:03:57,540 --> 00:03:59,279
那里只放嘻哈歌手德雷克的歌
that only plays Drake.

105
00:03:59,279 --> 00:04:03,060
这是我们最终的最高报价
So here's our offer, best and final.

106
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:04,140
什么报价
Offer for what?

107
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:05,860
买下你们公司的报价
For your company.

108
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:06,940
我们想买下你们
We want to buy you out.

109
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,000
不好意思 我们以为你们只是来
I'm sorry, we thought that you were here to just,

110
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,060
搜集信息
you know, get information.

111
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,341
给我滚出去
Get out of here!

112
00:04:12,341 --> 00:04:13,740
爸爸 不如让我来沟通吧
Dad, if you would just let me speak --

113
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:14,920
你以为自己是谁
Who do you think you are,

114
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:16,620
大步走进来自以为是一群大老板
marching in here like a bunch of hotshots?

115
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:17,959
为什么没人穿袜子
And why is nobody wearing socks?!

116
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:20,560
血压别这么高 老人家
Ooh, lower the B.P., O.G.

117
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,000
我们其实算是在帮你们一个大忙
We're actually trying to do you a favor.

118
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:24,500
我认为是你们没搞清楚
Okay, I think you have this twisted.

119
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:27,520
这间公司在你们所有人出生前就成立了
This company has been around since before you all were born.

120
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:29,860
或许除了他 他是怎么回事
Except for maybe him. How is he part of this?

121
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,760
这家伙吗 为了显得年龄多样化雇的
This guy? That's our over-40 diversity hire.

122
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:36,080
我们已经开发出了智能衣柜技术
Listen, we have developed smart-closet technology

123
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:37,980
你们这种公司迟早会被淘汰
that's gonna make places like this obsolete.

124
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:40,040
我们是给你们机会
We are giving you a chance

125
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,500
在还有优势时全身而退
to get out while you're still ahead.

126
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:45,240
说到全身而退 给我滚出去
Speaking of which -- Get out of here!

127
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:47,098
那好 我的出价48小时后失效
Okay. Offer's good for 48 hours.

128
00:04:47,098 --> 00:04:48,600
用说两次"滚出去"吗
Two get out of heres?

129
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,320
你能相信这些小流氓吗
You believe these punks?

130
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,760
他们怎么敢进行那么多目光交流
I mean, what was with all this eye contact?

131
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:55,140
我那个年代 书呆子会规规矩矩地盯着鞋
In my day, nerds had the decency to stare at their shoes!

132
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,360
他们的网站看起来挺正规的
Their website looks legitimate.

133
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:59,100
他们还有不少大客户
I mean, they've got some pretty great clients.

134
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:00,660
等一下 那是玛格丽特吗
Wait a second, is that Margaret?

135
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:03,240
她在那工作 肯定是他们挖走了她
She's working there. They must have poached her.

136
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,620
他们肯定给她洗脑了
Brainwashed her, is what they did.

137
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:05,680
玛格丽特很容易上当
Margaret is very vulnerable.

138
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:07,440
我曾经无数次把她从邪教
I've had to rescue her a bunch of times

139
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,300
和安利金字塔营销中救出来
from cults and an Amway pyramid.

140
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,060
快 去把我们的姑娘救回来
Come on. Let's get our girl back!

141
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,740
你都骑出大峡谷了
You were all the way out of the Grand Canyon

142
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:15,780
才发现我不在驴上
before you realized no one was on my donkey.

143
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,800
不过 当然 我们去救玛格丽特
But, sure, let's go save Margaret.

144
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:22,920
妈 我的恐龙派对看起来好棒
Mom, my dinosaur party looks amazing!

145
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:24,660
可我们订的是那个房间
But we're in that room.

146
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,460
肯定是有人在我们隔壁办了恐龙派对
Somebody must've done another dinosaur party right next to us.

147
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:29,334
歌洛莉亚
Gloria?

148
00:05:29,334 --> 00:05:32,106
唐娜·邓肯医生
Doctor Donna Duncan.

149
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:34,200
记得我的继子迪格比吗
You remember my stepson, Digby.

150
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,920
他更喜欢不用语言来交流
He prefers nonverbal communication.

151
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,480
这是你的派对吗
This is your party?

152
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,360
你瞧 我看到你预定
You see, I saw that you had signed up

153
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,780
要给杰西卡老师带的班开派对
to throw a party for Miss Jessica's class,

154
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,320
所以我想给伊莱恩老师带的班也办个小派对
so I thought I'd throw a little party for Miss Elaine.

155
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:49,360
它能喷完火后朝整个房间喷糖果哦
It belches fire and then shoots candy all over the room.

156
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:55,640
妹子
Hey, girl, hey!

157
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:56,960
我不会陪你去公路旅行的
I'm not going on your road trip.

158
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:58,980
-什么 -卢克告诉我你一直在煽动他
- What? - Luke told me that you've been hounding him

159
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:00,640
因为你不想独自开车横跨全国
because you don't want to drive cross-country alone.

160
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:02,180
我只是想帮你个忙
Oh, I'm just trying to do you a favor.

161
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,900
你要去孟斐斯开会
You're going to a conference in Memphis.

162
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:05,320
我只要多开12小时车程就行了
It's only 12 hours out of my way.

163
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:07,780
你不必害怕
Hey, no need to be afraid.

164
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:08,640
害什么怕
Afraid?

165
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:12,600
曼尼 我是个穿低胸上衣的漂亮女孩
Manny, I'm a pretty girl who wears low-cut tops.

166
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,680
我知道19岁男孩害怕时是什么神情
I know what a scared 19-year-old boy looks like.

167
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:19,200
老兄 你五年级时带排箫去学校
Dude, you brought a pan flute to the fifth grade.

168
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,700
你给比你人气高超多的女孩唱小夜曲
You serenade girls who are way out of your league.

169
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,940
你胆子很大 你没问题的
You're a baller. You got this.

170
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,460
-多谢鼓励 -随时乐意效劳
- Thanks. - Anytime.

171
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:34,600
曼尼 曼尼 你这是绑架
Manny. Manny, this is kidnapping.

172
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:37,640
他们办公室真大
Wow, this office is huge.

173
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:40,816
刚盖的 这里过去是史怀伯格百货商店
Just placed it. This used to be Schweinberg's department store.

174
00:06:40,816 --> 00:06:42,960
那边是电视墙
Wall of TVs over there.

175
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:45,060
我当时差点撞翻了芝士火锅样品
I almost knocked down the display of fondue pots

176
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:48,020
因为我看到他们让芭芭拉·沃尔特斯报新闻
when I saw they were letting Barbara Walters anchor the news.

177
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,720
看看是谁来了
Look who's here!

178
00:06:49,730 --> 00:06:52,660
你们一定不会后悔接受我们的出价
You are not gonna regret taking our offer.

179
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:53,340
我们去庆祝吧
Let's celebrate.

180
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:54,560
我们不是来卖公司的
We're not here to sell.

181
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:56,280
我们是来带玛格丽特回家的
We're here to bring Margaret home.

182
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:56,920
玛格丽特是谁
Who's Margaret?

183
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:58,520
玛吉
Margie!

184
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,120
小玛吉
Margie-Marge!

185
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:02,820
他们怎么骗你来的
How did they get you?

186
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,760
你还独自去宠物店瞎逛吗
Are you still wandering around alone in pet stores?

187
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:08,960
我告诉过你 这些邪教专拉这种人
I've told you, that's the kind of person these cults target!

188
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,700
我喜欢这里
I like it here.

189
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:14,700
他们有能做各种汽水的机器
They have one of those machines that makes every kind of soda.

190
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,180
可你有糖尿病 还是个成年人
But you're diabetic. And a grown-up.

191
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:19,820
既然你们来了 不如我带你们看看新型号
You know, since you're here, why don't I show you the new model?

192
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:20,999
来 过来
Come here. Come over here.

193
00:07:20,999 --> 00:07:25,403
过来 这是伊瑟拉视界精英
Come here. This is the EzraVision Elitist.

194
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:26,660
站在这
Stand right over there.

195
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:27,820
面向前面
Face forward.

196
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:29,700
下午好 伊瑟拉
Good afternoon, Ezra.

197
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,923
下午好 需要什么帮助吗
Good afternoon. How may I help you?

198
00:07:31,923 --> 00:07:32,693
那是什么
What is that?

199
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:34,440
伊瑟拉 进行全身扫描
Ezra, full body scan.

200
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:38,380
-来吧 -扫描完成 搜索衣橱
- Here we go. - Scan complete. Searching wardrobe.

201
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:40,519
根据今天的天气预报
Based on today's weather forecast,

202
00:07:40,519 --> 00:07:42,313
这是您的最佳着装
here's your optimal outfit.

203
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:43,840
看看标牌
Check the label.

204
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,560
-正是我的尺寸 -没错
- Just my size. - Yes, it is.

205
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,640
这就是衣柜的未来
See, this is the future of closets --

206
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:50,780
自动化 智能化
automated, intelligent --

207
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:52,820
七十年代的"情绪衣柜"也是这么宣传的
That's what they said about the "mood closet" in the '70s,

208
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:54,660
-我亲手送它入土了 -他真暴躁
- and I buried them. - Very cranky.

209
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:57,120
是的 不过他赢得了暴躁的权利
Yes, but he has earned the right to be cranky,

210
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:59,859
因为我父亲是这一行的巨人
because my father is a giant in this industry,

211
00:07:59,859 --> 00:08:02,740
并且他为了来这今天没吃冰淇淋三明治
and he had to skip his ice-cream sandwich today to come here.

212
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:05,180
尼克 该玩激光枪战了
Nick, it's time for laser tag.

213
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,480
太棒了 你们知道吗
Yes! You know what?

214
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,480
无论最终结果如何 裤子你留着
No matter how it shakes out, you can keep the pants.

215
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:11,200
-我送你了 -我们走
- Those are on me. - Let's go!

216
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:12,320
我们快走
Let's get the hell out of here.

217
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:14,180
等等 爸 我
Hang on, Dad. I...

218
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:15,860
我和你一样不喜欢这些书呆
I don't like these dorks any more than you do,

219
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:17,640
但他们有些想法可能很有前景
but they might be onto something.

220
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:19,120
你什么意思 你想卖公司吗
What are you saying? You want to sell?

221
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:21,500
不 我在考虑合并
No, I was thinking more of a merger.

222
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,000
我做了些调查
I did some digging,

223
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,960
他们生产不过来 订单排到两年后了
and they are two years behind on production.

224
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:26,900
他们需要我们的生产能力
They need our manufacturing,

225
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:30,118
而说实话 我们需要他们的科技
and frankly, we need their technology.

226
00:08:30,118 --> 00:08:32,560
不 不可能 谈话结束
Nope, not gonna happen. End of conversation.

227
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:32,900
非要这样吗
Really?

228
00:08:33,199 --> 00:08:35,560
我是在跟你讨论公司业务
I-I'm having a business discussion.

229
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:37,560
不是在商量一个新的睡觉时间
I am not negotiating a new bedtime.

230
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,540
我才不要找一个外人当合伙人
I'm not taking on an outside partner.

231
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:41,480
我懂了 因为你不太会处理合伙人关系
Oh, I get it, 'cause you're not very good with partners.

232
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:43,960
你让我当负责人得有九次了吧
I mean, you put me in charge, like, nine times,

233
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,400
但如果是个重要决定
but if it's an important decision,

234
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:46,800
我就得闭嘴
I should just shut up.

235
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:48,060
这能怪我吗
Well, I can't help it

236
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:49,920
我对这行有神一般的第六感
if I have a sixth sense about this business.

237
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,500
是衣柜选择了我
Closets chose me!

238
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,440
我的天啊
Oh, my gosh! Hey!

239
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:57,360
那边玩得超嗨的
It's going great over there, huh?

240
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:58,917
怎么回事 这些孩子做错事了吗
What's this? Are these kids in trouble?

241
00:08:58,917 --> 00:09:02,120
那个派对跟这个不一样 高档多了
That's a different, fancier party than this.

242
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:05,550
这里唯一好玩的就是那个金字塔 材料是...
The only fun thing I have is that pyramid made out of --

243
00:09:05,550 --> 00:09:08,176
小卡 看你那个巨婴外甥干了什么
Ay, Cam, look what your giant baby nephew did!

244
00:09:08,176 --> 00:09:10,580
对 但你要知道 这不是他的错
Yeah, but you know, it's not his fault.

245
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:12,880
他的身型是同龄孩子的三倍
He's three times the size of a child his age.

246
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:14,369
还有你知道吗 有些塔克家的孩子
And you know what, some Tucker boys

247
00:09:14,369 --> 00:09:17,073
会很早就经历痛苦的快速成长期
have a young growth spurt that's no picnic.

248
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:18,880
我小时候得上法院证明年龄才能打少年棒球联盟
I had to go to court to play Little League.

249
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,120
卡梅隆 亲爱的
Cameron, sweetie!

250
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:22,920
我就觉得听到了你的声音
I thought I heard your voice

251
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:26,520
穿过这个无趣安静的...
cutting through the joyless silence of this...

252
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:27,460
我本来想说派对
I want to say party,

253
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:29,160
但我怕听起来像是讽刺
but I'm afraid it will sound sarcastic.

254
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:30,460
你们是朋友吗
You guys are friends?

255
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,760
我们在同一家发廊做头发
Uh, well, we go to the same blowout parlor, yeah.

256
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,560
等等 你花钱请我吹头
Wait a minute, did you pay for my Belizian blowout

257
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,920
就是为了让我告诉你歌洛莉亚的派对详情
just so I would shout the details of Gloria's party

258
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:38,260
好让自己能赢过她吗
so you could outdo her?

259
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:40,420
你可算明白了
Oh, look at you catching on.

260
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:42,547
孩子们 很抱歉吵醒你们了
Kids, sorry to wake you.

261
00:09:42,547 --> 00:09:44,920
但我要把这些腕带留在这里
But I'm gonna leave these wristbands here

262
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,900
以防你们想来坐我们的过山车
in case any of you want to come ride our roller coaster.

263
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:49,720
真正的机械过山车
The mechanical kind,

264
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:51,680
不是你们走进这里后
not the emotional one you've been on

265
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,940
在心中经历的心情过山车
since you came through these doors.

266
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:55,000
给我滚出去
Get out of here!

267
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:56,980
不是你 不是你 不是你
Not you, not you, not you.

268
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:58,740
天啊 比我想象的还糟糕
Oh, God, this is worse than I thought.

269
00:09:58,900 --> 00:10:00,280
有好多眼睛正盯着我
There are so many eyes on me.

270
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:01,220
当然了
I mean, yes, sure,

271
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:03,479
那些独眼巨人让眼睛数目少了点 不过还是多
less because of all the cyclopses, but still.

272
00:10:03,479 --> 00:10:05,362
你可以的 提起你的精[灵]神
You can do this. Elf up.

273
00:10:05,362 --> 00:10:08,825
我最喜欢的两个莱茵少女 琳达 凯伦
My two favorite Rhine maidens! Linda! Karen!

274
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:10,400
之前卖了她们一套复式公寓
Sold them a duplex.

275
00:10:10,713 --> 00:10:13,900
我了个妈妈咪啊
Sweet home Alduzzarna,

276
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:16,680
《神剑之战》第五季里的制傻者
it's the Foolmaker from "Clash of Swords" season five!

277
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:18,860
我只看到了第三季 有点困惑 跟我说说
I'm only on season three. I feel lost. Help me.

278
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:20,299
好吧 在无花果盛宴上
Oh, okay. During the Feast of Figs,

279
00:10:20,299 --> 00:10:22,320
森林王子把漫游者米苟拉夫驱逐到
the Forest Prince banished Migolaf the Wanderer

280
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,937
遗弃之国境外
to the outer reaches of The Forsaken Realm.

281
00:10:23,937 --> 00:10:26,980
米苟拉夫伏击了依果达然侏儒
Migolaf waylaid the Iguodalan Dwarves

282
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,960
并诅咒那位高级牧师永远痴傻
and cursed the high cleric to an eternity of feeble-mindedness

283
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:32,280
用的就是这支强大的权杖 它被人称
using the mighty scepter known as...

284
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:34,847
"制傻者" 我要拍张自拍
The Foolmaker. I got to get a selfie.

285
00:10:34,847 --> 00:10:38,120
小心 小心
Ooh, careful! Careful!

286
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,600
天啊 好吧
Oh, boy. Okay.

287
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:40,900
还好这不是真货
Good thing it's not the real one

288
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:42,600
不然我这后半辈子都要受诅咒
or I'd be cursed to spend the rest of my days

289
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,500
变成一个碎碎念的白痴了
as a bumbling idiot.

290
00:10:44,278 --> 00:10:46,500
你要生一个煮粥女仆 还是
Aw, are you gonna have a little porridge maiden

291
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,247
一个小勇士
or a little warrior?

292
00:10:47,247 --> 00:10:49,980
我没怀孕 白痴
I'm not pregnant, dipwad.

293
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:51,260
菲尔 你为什么这么说
Phil, why would you say that?!

294
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,400
我不知道啊 脱口而出
I don't know, it just came out.

295
00:10:52,964 --> 00:10:55,540
因为这支制傻者...
I mean, The Foolmaker --

296
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:57,140
你没有被诅咒 好吗 那是道具 不是真的
You're not cursed, okay? It's a prop. It's not real.

297
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:58,700
好吧 见面座谈会在这边
All right. The panel's this way.

298
00:10:59,791 --> 00:11:01,640
兄弟 你的鳞片铠甲太屌了
Hey, man. Sick scale armor!

299
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:03,860
真的吗 你真觉得吗 配披风不会太夸张吗
Oh, really? You think so? It's not too much with the cape?

300
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:06,180
我想要那种既可以赴宴也可以参战的
I wanted something that would go from feast to battle.

301
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:07,238
-你做到了 -太好了
- Crushed it. - Yes!

302
00:11:07,238 --> 00:11:09,100
我们要拍一张年度北境大合照
Oh, we're about to take our annual Norph group photo.

303
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:10,240
-你要来吗 -当然
- You coming? -Yes, yes!

304
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:11,660
菲尔 我们要拍一张照
Phil, we're taking a pic--

305
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:12,900
抱歉 我跟我朋友走散了
Oh, I'm sorry. I lost my friend.

306
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,758
我们大多数都是一个人来的 没必要假装
Hey, most of us come alone. You don't have to pretend.

307
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,606
我
I -- Th--

308
00:11:17,748 --> 00:11:20,054
太好了 问答环节刚刚开始
Oh, great, the Q&A's just starting.

309
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:20,400
米奇
Mitch?

310
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:21,899
这是个非常非常好的问题
That's a very, very good question...

311
00:11:21,899 --> 00:11:24,300
-米奇尔 -问题的答案是
- Mitchell? - ...and the answer to that is...

312
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:26,340
可怕的食人怪牙齿 你怎么弄来的
Scary ogre teeth. Where'd you get those?

313
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:28,160
我的亲生父母给的
I'm guessing my birth parents.

314
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:30,000
很抱歉
I'm so sorry.

315
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:33,020
我怎么就不能闭嘴呢
Why can't I just shut up?

316
00:11:33,267 --> 00:11:35,900
抱歉 是我说太久了吗
Sorry, was I going on too long?

317
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:38,220
我没有
I didn't --

318
00:11:40,592 --> 00:11:41,624
你是乔尔.L.L.罗根
You're Joel L.L. Logan.

319
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:44,340
你有什么问题 朋友
What's your question, friend?

320
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:46,080
别害羞
Don't be shy.

321
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,680
虽然的确是我创造了这王国
I may have created this kingdom,

322
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,900
但我们都是这个王国的继承人
but we're all fellow heirs to it.

323
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:50,560
对吧
Isn't that right?

324
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:55,900
那样的话 罗根先生
In that case, Mr. Logan...

325
00:11:56,702 --> 00:11:57,819
我在一个粉丝页面上看到
Uh, I read on a fan page

326
00:11:57,819 --> 00:12:00,900
本季季末会出现一个莫兹果人
there's gonna be a Mozgovian uprising in the season finale

327
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:03,240
消灭所有统治阶级
that'll wipe out the entire ruling class,

328
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:07,122
包括凶残地斩首正义之子阿德巴约
including the gruesome beheading of Adebayo the Righteous.

329
00:12:09,222 --> 00:12:11,880
等等 你 你要杀死阿德巴约吗
Wait, a-are you -- are you gonna kill Adebayo?

330
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:13,880
什么 不不不
What? No, no.

331
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:16,080
谁是 谁 谁是阿德巴约啊
Who's -- Who -- Who's Adebayo?

332
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:18,160
老天爷啊 看来是真的
Oh, dear lord. It is true.

333
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:21,140
你个蠢蛋 为什么要问他这个
You fool! Why would you ask him that?!

334
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:23,620
我们不上剧透网站是有原因的
We all stay off of spoiler sites for a reason!

335
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:27,440
这是我唯一还在追的剧 你就这么毁了
This show is the only thing I've got going on and you ruined it!

336
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:31,060
主办单位准你们带晶球入场吗
They let you bring your spheres?!

337
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:33,300
他们把我的镊子都没收了
They took away my tweezers!

338
00:12:37,870 --> 00:12:38,820
曼尼
Manny?

339
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:40,400
这是努斯鲍姆太太给的支票
This is the check Mrs. Nussbaum gave me

340
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:41,560
要我把她的车开到特拉华
to drive her car to Delaware.

341
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,220
如果你跟我走 它就是你的了
It's yours if you come with me.

342
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,060
-好 -等下 什么
- Okay. - Wait, what?

343
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:47,220
海莉已经警告我你会这么问
Well, Haley already warned me you'd be asking

344
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,320
我想 去就去吧
and I thought, sure.

345
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:50,480
反正也顺路去我最爱的研究所
My favorite research institute is on the way.

346
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:53,220
我可以带上我的风向袋和气压表
And I could bring my windsock and barometer

347
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:55,460
去做我正在进行的天气建模项目
for that new weather modeling project I've been noodling with.

348
00:12:57,460 --> 00:13:00,720
我不禁注意到你枕头上有好多散落的头发
I couldn't help noticing a lot of loose hairs on your pillow

349
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:04,560
还有一叠做完的数独书
and a stack of fully completed Sudoku books.

350
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:07,040
你这个夏天不是应该放松吗
Weren't you supposed to be taking it easy this summer?

351
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:08,440
不考虑学习 项目
No school, no projects --

352
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:09,820
对 我特喜欢这生活
Yeah, I'm loving it.

353
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:11,480
那我打开你的衣柜
What are the chances I open your dresser

354
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:13,240
会不会找到一本日历 上面有三天打叉
and find a calendar with three X'd out days

355
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:15,580
开学的日期上有大大的红色的圈
and a giant red circle around the date school starts again?

356
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:17,580
你不了解我
You don't know me.

357
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:21,360
你正在面临你所畏惧的挑战
Look, you're facing a challenge that scares you,

358
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:23,700
但你内心也知道你需要正面迎敌
but you know in your heart you need to take it on.

359
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:25,780
因为它能帮助你成长
Because it'll help you grow

360
00:13:25,780 --> 00:13:28,420
成为一个更强大 生活更平衡的人
and become a stronger, more balanced person.

361
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:33,180
我当然知道你是对的 但很难
Of course I know you're right, but it's hard!

362
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,600
有人在外面探索星球
People are out there discovering planets,

363
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,360
我却在家做网上的白痴小测验
and I'm in here doing BuzzFeed quizzes.

364
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:38,860
如果我是披头士的一员 我会是谁
Like if I were to be a Beatle, who would I be?

365
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:41,060
我会是林戈 谁在乎呢 曼尼
I'd be Ringo. Who cares, Manny?!

366
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:41,980
曼尼
Manny?

367
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:51,020
我可能丢失了菲尔 但找到了我的同类
I may have lost Phil, but I found my people.

368
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:52,920
舞蹈轻而易举
And the choreography was a snap.

369
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:56,788
基本上就是大河之舞穿插着霍拉舞
It's basically a river dance, uh, crossed with the hora.

370
00:13:57,220 --> 00:13:58,980
我从卡塔丽娜之间带回了消息
I bring news from the Catalina Room!

371
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,620
黑影笼罩了这个帝国
A dark shadow has fallen upon the kingdom.

372
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:04,102
神明会因此而动怒
The gods will not be pleased by this --

373
00:14:04,102 --> 00:14:05,260
快说 盖里
Just get to it, Gary!

374
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:06,856
有个家伙剧透了季终集
Some dingus just spoiled the finale!

375
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,940
必须惩罚他
This shall not go unpunished!

376
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:10,700
咱们找他去
Let's get him!

377
00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:18,120
你去哪了 我等了好久
Where have you been? I've been waiting forever.

378
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:19,940
我很生气 我需要走一走
I was angry. I needed to take a walk

379
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:22,040
这样才能忘了你有多固执
so I could forget how pigheaded you can be.

380
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,080
你想再走一圈吗
You want to take another lap?

381
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:25,920
爸 我是对的
Dad, I am right about this.

382
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:28,540
总有一天尼克能想出怎么保证供货
Eventually Nick is gonna figure out how to keep up with demand,

383
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:30,360
那到时候我们该何去何从
and then where are we gonna be?

384
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:33,001
我知道你的风格是坚持到底
I know your style has always been just tough it out

385
00:14:33,001 --> 00:14:35,040
击退每一个威胁
and -- and beat back every threat --

386
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:35,820
不是 克莱尔
That's not it, Claire.

387
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:37,319
你是对的 我们打不过他们
You're right. We can't beat these guys.

388
00:14:37,319 --> 00:14:39,548
从长远看合并才是唯一可行的办法
A merger's the only long-term play.

389
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:44,160
我只是不知道该把自己放在什么位置
I just don't know who I am in there.

390
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:45,497
什么
What?

391
00:14:45,497 --> 00:14:48,094
他们都25岁左右 飞驰在那什么上
They're all 25, zippin' around on their...

392
00:14:48,397 --> 00:14:49,697
平衡车吗
The hoverboards?

393
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,560
那我成了什么 可爱的老家伙
What's that make me, the cute old guy?

394
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:52,160
还是吉祥物
The mascot?

395
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,560
"老普里契特在厕所呢
"Old man Pritchett's in the men's room.

396
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:57,220
快去看他又对着自动水龙头乱骂"
Let's go watch him cuss out the automatic faucets again."

397
00:14:57,561 --> 00:14:58,554
爸
Aw, Dad.

398
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:01,000
我不能保证
I can't promise that

399
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,080
你在那栋楼里不会感到自己老了
you wouldn't feel old in that building,

400
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:05,200
但从外面看来
but from the outside looking in,

401
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,760
你完全镇得住
I mean, you're the guy

402
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:09,800
一群年纪只有自己三分之一的小屁孩
who's holding his own with kids a third his age.

403
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:14,060
你就好比是衣柜界的托尼·班尼特
That makes you like the... the Tony Bennett of closets.

404
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:16,920
我和你说过我曾在罗马和他坐同班电梯吧
I told you I took an elevator with him in Rome, right?

405
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:18,720
你说过 你知道吗
Yeah, you did. And you know what,

406
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:20,060
那栋楼里有好多人
in that building there's a bunch of people

407
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:21,840
还没听过这个故事呢
who have never heard that story.

408
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:24,440
他是不是还带了只吉娃娃
Did he have a Chihuahua with him?

409
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:25,720
-貂 -貂
- A mink. - A mink?

410
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,260
-一只活貂 -没错
- A live mink. - Yeah.

411
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:28,740
-可有范儿了 -没错
- All class. - Yeah.

412
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:30,500
可能我觉得有点受威胁吧
It's just a little intimidating.

413
00:15:31,019 --> 00:15:33,380
你觉得他们不会怕你吗
You don't think they're gonna be scared of you?

414
00:15:33,380 --> 00:15:36,340
别啊 爸 你看他们
Come on. Dad, look at them.

415
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:40,140
无论他们的衣柜帮他们挑出了什么毒舌T恤
I don't care what ironic T-shirt their closets pick out for them.

416
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,700
他们本质上始终还是死书呆
Underneath, they're still nerds.

417
00:15:48,279 --> 00:15:49,200
真是服了你
I can't.

418
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,620
是啦 我想我应该能行吧
Yeah, this might be okay.

419
00:15:53,415 --> 00:15:55,223
我想见他 让我过去 让我过去
I want to see him. Let me through, let me through!

420
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:57,480
你就是剧透的家伙吗
You're the spoiler?

421
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:58,866
我不是故意的
I didn't do it on purpose!

422
00:15:58,866 --> 00:16:00,680
是制傻者害的
It was The Foolmaker!

423
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:02,120
权杖只是个道具好吗
The scepter is a prop, okay?

424
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,520
你是自己被心里暗示所影响了
It's just the power of suggestion.

425
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:06,320
米奇尔 他们想收走我的全通票
Mitchell, they want to take away my all-access pass.

426
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:08,050
-你得帮我 -你认识这个败类吗
- You've got to help me. - You know this scoundrel?

427
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:09,748
算吧 我们两家的孩子好像在同学校...
Uh, yeah, I think our kids go to school with one --

428
00:16:09,748 --> 00:16:11,600
-米奇尔 -好吧 我认识他
- Mitchell! ?- Okay yes, yes -- yes, I know him.

429
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:12,660
-我认识他 -他们是恶魔
- I know him! - They're monsters.

430
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:15,096
他们一直朝我丢乔巴尼连枷球
They've been pelting me with Chobani flail spheres.

431
00:16:15,096 --> 00:16:16,600
等下 乔巴尼 那个酸奶品牌吗
Wait -- Ch-Chobani, like the yoghurt?

432
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,620
剧在第四季时接了商业植入
The show took on corporate sponsors in season four.

433
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:22,540
不是吧 盖里
Seriously, Gary?

434
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,160
我帮忙你组建了牌组呢
I helped you build a deck!

435
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:26,228
停 停 我们在做什么
Okay, stop, stop it! What are we doing, huh?

436
00:16:26,257 --> 00:16:27,830
北境人是这样的吗
Is this how Norphs behave?

437
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:29,108
其实我们还挺好战的
Actually, we're quite war-like.

438
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:32,900
看 看 这个人他犯了错
Look, look, this man, he made a mistake,

439
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,760
但如果我们驱逐他
but if we banish him,

440
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:38,320
我们就和这些年来羞辱咱们的人一样了
we're no better than the people who shamed us all these years,

441
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:40,820
他们在团队运动时最后选咱们
who -- who picked us last for team sports,

442
00:16:41,180 --> 00:16:44,480
群发律师协会舞会邀请邮件时漏掉咱们
who left us off of group e-mails about bar association dances.

443
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:48,500
我们是怪咖 奇葩 怪胎
We're all oddballs and misfits and weirdos,

444
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:51,940
但这里最好的地方就是包容一切
but the great thing about this place is we all belong,

445
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:54,100
特别是这个善良的人
especially this good man,

446
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:57,520
是他给了我战胜恐惧的勇气
who gave me the courage to conquer my fear

447
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:59,580
让我成为这个团体的一部分
and become part of this community.

448
00:17:00,260 --> 00:17:01,500
让我们欢迎他回来
Let's welcome him back.

449
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:03,180
红色的 盖里
The red one, Gary!

450
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:07,420
那个恐龙在哪
Where is that dinosaur?

451
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:09,340
我十分希望我没有
I certainly hope I don't

452
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:11,000
一不小心关了灯
accidentally turn off the lights.

453
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:13,940
身为一名同性恋 我认识市里所有派对策划人
As a gay man, I know every party planner in town.

454
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:16,440
所以我发了条群短信 我也真撞了大运
So I sent out a group text, and as luck would have it,

455
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:18,900
我朋友罗纳多刚好结束一场儿童的小飞侠派对
my friend Ronaldo was wrapping up a kid's Peter Pan party.

456
00:17:18,900 --> 00:17:21,060
我就说"你的派对有什么都带过来吧"
And I said, "Send me whatever you got."

457
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,540
我好像听到音乐啦
I think I hear some music!

458
00:17:24,616 --> 00:17:27,100
失踪的小男孩们都在哪啊
Where my lost boys at?!

459
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:28,560
这是什么鬼啊
What the hell is this?!

460
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:31,419
你不是说你在一场儿童的小飞侠派对吗
You said you were at a kid's Peter Pan party?

461
00:17:31,419 --> 00:17:34,700
不是不是 我是说"尔铜的小飞侠派对"
No, no, no. I said, "Kit's Peter Pan party."

462
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:36,498
尔铜叔第11次办50岁大寿了
It's his 11th time turning 50.

463
00:17:36,498 --> 00:17:39,120
大家闭上眼睛 别看
Close your eyes! No! Don't look at that!

464
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:40,380
拜托了 大家对不起
Please, I'm so sorry!

465
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:42,380
够了 够了
Enough! Enough!

466
00:17:42,780 --> 00:17:44,760
大家都出去 小孩子们也出去
Everybody out! Even the kids!

467
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:47,580
我坚持不下去了 你们去有趣派对那边吧
I can't fight this anymore. Go to the nice party!

468
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:49,220
跟着仙女娘娘过去吧
Just follow the fairy!

469
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:53,040
她是说我 不是大家娘 冷静
She meant me. Everybody calm down.

470
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,498
今天谢谢你了
Thank you so much for today.

471
00:17:55,498 --> 00:17:56,793
要我自己肯定坚持不下去
I-I never would've gone through with it

472
00:17:56,793 --> 00:17:58,495
都多亏了你的鼓舞
if you hadn't inspired me.

473
00:17:58,840 --> 00:17:59,600
我鼓舞了你吗
I inspired you?

474
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:00,920
等等
Wait.

475
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:03,402
在第三册中 高等祭司
In book the third, the high cleric

476
00:18:03,402 --> 00:18:05,340
成功克服制傻者的诅咒
overcomes the curse of the Foolmaker

477
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:06,640
靠的就是纯真之心
by being pure of heart

478
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:08,960
之后他成为了伟大的人民鼓舞者
and goes on to be a great inspirer of people.

479
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:09,940
你觉得...
Do you think --

480
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,900
你看起来好阴郁
You seem glum.

481
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:19,900
或许你该把你的热忱放在别的方向
Perhaps you should be turning your passions elsewhere.

482
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:23,320
你说得对 我要回去读兽医
You're right. I'm going back to vet school.

483
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:25,540
我也该长大了
It's about time I grew up.

484
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:28,735
我对不起你 歌洛莉亚
I'm sorry, Gloria.

485
00:18:28,735 --> 00:18:30,580
没事啦 我不生气
It's okay. I'm not mad.

486
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:31,681
派对怎么没了
What happened to the party?

487
00:18:31,681 --> 00:18:33,618
被小卡给毁了
Cam ruined it two ways.

488
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:36,780
我只是想帮乔办一个好的派对
I just wanted a nice party for Joe.

489
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:40,480
能帮孩子把一切做到尽善尽美的日子很短
There's only so long that you can make things perfect for them.

490
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:42,680
突然有天 他们就要离巢
Suddenly, they move on.

491
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:43,859
他们某天早上起来
They wake up one morning

492
00:18:43,859 --> 00:18:47,220
就说要独自开车横跨全国
and they want to drive cross-country all alone.

493
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:48,357
对 曼尼
Oh, right, Manny.

494
00:18:48,357 --> 00:18:51,620
我知道你在害怕 但你应该感到自豪啊
I know you're scared, but your should feel proud.

495
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:53,380
你把一个...
You took kind of a...

496
00:18:53,824 --> 00:18:55,140
你可以直说 一个小怪胎
You can say it -- a weird kid.

497
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:57,080
一个小怪胎养育成了一个
A weird kid, and turned him into somebody

498
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:58,560
对自己感到自信果敢
so comfortable with himself

499
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:01,980
愿意去开启一段挺大冒险的男子汉
that he's willing to take on a pretty big adventure.

500
00:19:02,184 --> 00:19:03,580
谢谢你 小卡
Thank you, Cam.

501
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:04,740
我也想有这样的教育
I wish I had that.

502
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:06,020
我小时候也是个小怪胎
I mean, I was a weird kid

503
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,880
但我的家庭只让我觉得自己更怪了
whose family only made him feel weirder.

504
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:10,100
我一直到今天才有这份自信与勇气
I mean, it took until today to do an adventure

505
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:12,258
做到我在曼尼那个年纪就想去做的冒险
that I have wanted to do since I was Manny's age.

506
00:19:12,258 --> 00:19:14,737
我去了英雄展
I-I went to Hero-Con.

507
00:19:14,780 --> 00:19:15,738
没穿戏服吧
Not in costume?

508
00:19:15,738 --> 00:19:16,957
穿了 菲茨宝
Affirmative, Fizbo.

509
00:19:16,957 --> 00:19:18,080
好吧 那如果你喜欢这些
Okay, if this is something you're into,

510
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,440
你为什么从不跟我说呢
why haven't you ever told me?

511
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:20,600
我从没跟任何人说过
I haven't told anyone.

512
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:22,780
我试过跟我妈说过一次
I mean, I tried with my mom once,

513
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:25,217
但我临阵怂了 最后跟她说我是同性恋
but I chickened out and told her I was gay instead.

514
00:19:25,217 --> 00:19:27,240
那会儿我自己都还没确定性向呢
And I-I wasn't even sure at that point.

515
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:30,520
为什么有这么多家长可以教育错孩子的方式啊
Why are there so many ways for a parent to break a kid?

516
00:19:31,399 --> 00:19:33,175
-抱抱 -不 别 别啊
- Hug! - No, no, no!

517
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:41,360
这让我好担心这个小伙子啊
Aw, you know, it makes me worried for this little guy.

518
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:43,640
我爱我的爸妈
I love my parents,

519
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:46,740
但是他们当年也不太会教...
but they weren't exactly the best when I was...

520
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:48,440
还这么大时的我
when I was this.

521
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:53,440
去玩吧
Go play.

522
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:58,240
米奇尔 我为你今天勇敢追梦
Mitchell, I'm, uh, proud of the risk you took today

523
00:19:58,240 --> 00:19:59,460
感到十分骄傲
following your heart.

524
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:01,522
你应该多多这样
You should do more of that.

525
00:20:01,522 --> 00:20:03,712
小卡 我们该收留卡尔吗
Cam, should Cal live with us?

526
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:05,760
应该
He should.

527
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:07,740
很好
Very well.

528
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:09,960
抱歉我们迟到了 堵车嘛
Sorry we're late. Traffic, you know.

529
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:11,600
我一直叫你用防堵车导航软件
I keep telling you to try Waze,

530
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:15,060
可你害怕使用新科技 其实你不该怕啊
but you're scared of technology, and you shouldn't be.

531
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,280
我们要将普里契特衣柜跟高科技公司合并
We're merging Pritchett's with a high-tech closet company.

532
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:18,180
太棒了
Excellent.

533
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:23,220
歌洛莉亚 你常提到你对腹语术很有兴趣
And, Gloria, you speak often of your passion for ventriloquism.

534
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:24,857
菲尔 今天已经够累了
It's been a long day, Phil.

535
00:20:25,820 --> 00:20:27,420
这一个需要多一点时间
This one needs more time.

536
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:29,436
旅途随笔
Notes from the road.

537
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:32,240
又名《我心中的美国》
Alternate title, The United States of me.

538
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:34,300
恐惧 是敌还是友
Fear -- Friend or Foe?

539
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:37,500
在小时候 我们被教要恐惧能伤我们的事物
As children, we're taught to fear what can hurt us.

540
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:42,100
但成年之后 我们却被要求能克服恐惧
But as adults, we're expected to conquer what we're afraid of.

541
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:45,680
所以什么是恐惧呢
So what are fears?

542
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,540
恐惧是让我们生存
Do they keep us alive?

543
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,400
还是让我们无法享受生活
Or do they keep us from living?

544
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:52,478
你把车道堵住了 赶紧开车走人吧
You're blocking the driveway. Hit the road already.

545
00:20:52,478 --> 00:20:53,800
好啦 我这就出发
Okay, I'm going.

546
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,200
杰
Jay.

547
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,180
快点啦
Hurry up.

548
00:20:58,180 --> 00:20:59,480
我们想回家了
We want to go home.

549
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:02,020
这破玩意他妈就是不灵啊
I can't get this damn thing to work.

550
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:04,159
惨了 是那种自动感应洗手台
Oh no, it's one of those automatic sinks.

551
00:21:04,159 --> 00:21:06,009
我觉得吧 你应该来个强行重启
You know what? You should do a hard reboot.

552
00:21:06,009 --> 00:21:08,120
先走回小便斗再重新走近洗手台
Go back to the urinal and reapproach.

553
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:08,860
里面发生什么事了
What's going on in there?

554
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:11,400
这玩意半滴都流不出来
I can't even get a trickle out of this thing!

555
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:13,820
不去想就尿得出了
I find not thinking about it helps.

556
00:21:14,020 --> 00:21:15,076
他是说水龙头
It's the sink.

557
00:21:15,076 --> 00:21:17,320
根本没道理 我都已经挥舞手臂
It makes no sensethat I'm waving my arms

558
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,240
挥得像在指挥飞机对接舱门那么夸张了
like I'm directing a plane into a gate!

559
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:20,680
他会把它砸了
He's gonna break it,

560
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:22,329
就像他把遥控器砸了一样
like he broke the remote control.

561
00:21:22,329 --> 00:21:25,030
真是... 那个纸巾架也是自动感应的
This is... the paper towel thing is automatic too.

562
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:26,220
老爸
Oh, dad.
